{"recall":{"defs":[["Ensemble","Combination of several base learners."],["Bagging","Bootstrap aggregating: vote over models trained on bootstrap samples."],["Random forest","Bagged decision trees with random feature subsets at each split."],["Boosting","Sequential training focusing on previous errors."],["AdaBoost","Boosting with exponential reweighting and α-weighted vote."],["Gradient boosting","Additive trees fitted to negative gradients of the loss."]],"formulas":["e_{ens}=\\sum_{i>n/2}\\binom ni\\varepsilon^i(1-\\varepsilon)^{n-i}","\\hat y=\\frac1M\\sum_mG_m(x)","\\alpha_i=\\frac12\\ln\\frac{1-\\varepsilon_i}{\\varepsilon_i}","w_j^{(i+1)}=\\frac{w_j^{(i)}}{Z_i}e^{-\\alpha_iy_jC_i(x_j)}","F_m(x)=F_{m-1}(x)+\\rho\\,h_m(x)"],"takeaways":["Ensembles need diverse members better than random.","Bagging/RF reduce variance; RF decorrelates trees by feature sampling.","AdaBoost: weighted error → α → reweight mistakes → weighted vote.","Gradient boosting fits residuals (negative gradients) with shrinkage.","XGBoost adds regularisation, missing-value handling and speed."],"confused":[["Bagging vs boosting","Parallel/variance vs sequential/bias."],["Bagging vs random forest","RF also samples features at each split."],["AdaBoost vs gradient boosting","Sample weights vs gradients."],["Version 1 vs version 2 AdaBoost","Average vs sum of misclassified weights."]],"minute":"An ensemble combines several base learners by voting or averaging; it beats its members when they are better than random and make independent errors. Bagging trains models in parallel on bootstrap samples (about 63% distinct records each) and votes, reducing variance. Random forests bag unpruned trees and sample a random subset of features at every split, decorrelating the trees and giving feature importances. Boosting trains sequentially: AdaBoost computes each member's weighted error ε, gives it a vote α = ½ ln((1 − ε)/ε), increases the weights of misclassified points and predicts by weighted vote. Gradient boosting starts from a constant and adds trees fitted to the pseudo-residuals, scaled by a learning rate; XGBoost is an optimised, regularised implementation."},"flashcards":[["No Free Lunch","No algorithm is always the most accurate"],["Weak learner","Only slightly better than random guessing"],["Diversity sources","Algorithms, hyperparameters, inputs, training sets"],["Fusion rules","Sum, weighted sum, median, min, max, product"],["Ensemble conditions","Independent members, each error < 0.5"],["Bagging","Bootstrap samples, parallel models, vote/average"],["Bootstrap coverage","≈ 63.2% distinct records"],["Random forest","Bagged unpruned trees + random p features per split"],["Boosting","Sequential; each model corrects the previous"],["AdaBoost α","$\\frac12\\ln\\frac{1-\\varepsilon}{\\varepsilon}$"],["AdaBoost update","$w\\cdot e^{\\pm\\alpha}/Z$ (+ if wrong)"],["AdaBoost prediction","$\\arg\\max_y\\sum\\alpha_j\\delta(C_j(x)=y)$"],["Gradient boosting step","$F_m=F_{m-1}+\\rho h_m$"],["Pseudo-residual","Negative gradient of the loss"],["Squared-loss residual","$y-F(x)$"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["e-single"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1","what"],"deep":["e-philosophy"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what"],"deep":["e-committee"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["e-diverse"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["e-combine"],"viz":["combinerLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["e-when"],"viz":["ensembleError"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what"],"deep":["e-types"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["e-bagging"],"viz":["baggingStumps"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["e-bagmodel"],"viz":["baggingStumps"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["e-bagex"],"viz":["baggingStumps"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6"],"deep":["e-bagbias"],"viz":["rfLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7","demo"],"deep":["e-rf"],"viz":["